---
source: crates/lighthouse-report/tests/it/agent.rs
expression: "render(Format::Agent, &findings, &gap(), &briefing)"
---
design/coupling  warn  internal/jit/compile.go:350:1
  owner:       jit::compile#function
  message:     function coordinates 14 collaborators in its package
  requirement: A function SHOULD NOT be a high fan-in/fan-out dependency hub or an oversized coordinator; such functions deserve review for responsibility and change propagation.
  context:     Fan-in, fan-out and statement count identify dependency hubs and high fan-out coordinators (Henry–Kafura). They are advisory signals rather than proof of a defect.
  evidence:    callees=["a","b c"] fan_in=2 fan_out=14
  expected:    valid go example `hub-ordinary-fan` (sample.go), canonical
                 package sample

                 func hub() {
                 	left()
                 	right()
                 }

                 func left()  {}
                 func right() {}

                 func a() { hub() }
                 func b() { hub() }
  fingerprint: 5da1c26
  resolve:     lighthouse review resolve 5da1c26 --judgment <pass|fail|notApplicable> [--suppress <justification>] [--reason <text>] --attributed-to agent:<id>

design/no-redundant-symbol  info (authored warn)  src/lib.rs:7:1
  owner:       m::helper#function
  message:     private helper has one caller
  requirement: A symbol SHOULD earn its existence by naming reusable behavior, a contract, an invariant, or a real abstraction; a forwarding wrapper or one-implementation private interface SHOULD be consolidated when it adds no distinct responsibility.
  context:     One-use helpers are reviewed semantically: extract them only when they name a concept, remove duplication, isolate an abstraction level, serve as a function value, or provide a test seam. A private forwarding wrapper that adds no policy is inlined; a private interface with one implementation is replaced with the concrete type until another implementation exists.
  expected:    valid rust example `rust-valid` (src/lib.rs), canonical
                 /// Part of the example.
                 pub struct Store {
                     closed: bool,
                     data: Vec<u8>,
                 }

                 impl Store {
                     fn load(&self, k: usize) -> u8 {
                         if self.closed {
                             return 0;
                         }
                         self.read(k)
                 ...
  fingerprint: 2e996a5
  resolve:     lighthouse review resolve 2e996a5 --judgment <pass|fail|notApplicable> [--suppress <justification>] [--reason <text>] --attributed-to agent:<id>

acme/custom  error  a.txt:1:1
  message:     custom finding
  fingerprint: c8dfae3

broken.go: incomplete: type error
judgments: fail=the finding is right; add `suppress` with a justification to leave it in place; pass=false positive: the code conforms; notApplicable=the decision does not apply here; a hint to narrow it
